# TypeScript

## Compiler settings

- `strict: false`, but `strictNullChecks: true` — honor null checks; do not weaken them
- `moduleResolution: "bundler"`, `jsx: "react-jsx"`, path root via `baseUrl: "src/"`
- Prefer imports like `core/...`, not deep relative `../../../` across layers

## Types vs interfaces

- Prefer **`type`** (especially `z.infer<typeof schema>`) over `interface`
- Domain input types come from Zod schemas in `src/core/validators/`
- Avoid inventing duplicate DTOs when a Zod schema already exists

```ts
// ✅ Existing pattern
export type VehicleSchema = z.infer<typeof createVehicleSchema>;
```

## Errors & validation

- Domain errors extend `AppError` (`Conflict`, `NotFound`, `Validation`) with `statusCode` + `code`
- Services validate with Zod (`.parse`), then call repositories
- Map unique violations via `isUniqueConstraintError` (Postgres `23505`) to `Conflict`
- API layer uses `handleApiError` for `AppError`, `ZodError` (422), and fallback 500

## Style notes

- No Prettier/ESLint config checked in yet; keep existing formatting (double quotes, trailing commas)
- Avoid `any` except local narrow helpers already present (e.g. unique-constraint check)
